# Deny-by-default for anything that could be personal.
#
# The asymmetry matters: a missed rule publishes someone's private life and
# their voice; an over-broad rule just means a file doesn't ship.
#
# NOTE: gitignore has NO trailing comments. A '#' only starts a comment at the
# START of a line. `secret.md   # explanation` is a literal pattern containing
# spaces and a hash, and matches nothing. Every comment here is on its own
# line for that reason - an earlier version of this file annotated patterns
# inline and silently protected none of them.
#
# Verify, don't assume:
#     git check-ignore -v core_memory.md
#     git add -A && git status --short

# ---- personal substrate: NEVER commit ----
# who the operator is: family, health, work, history
core_memory.md
# accrued memory from real conversations
accrued_memory.md
# her backstory, if she has one. Held back for two reasons: it is authored
# character content that belongs to whoever wrote it, and the one on this
# machine is the Sesame-derived origin, which is not ours to redistribute.
# origin.example.md ships in its place.
origin.md
# policy doc; describes sensitive disclosures by category
restricted.md
# imported conversation history
memory_corpus.jsonl
# FTS5 index built from it
memory_archive.db

# ---- biometrics: NEVER commit ----
# enrolled speaker embeddings
voiceprints.json
# recordings of the operator's voice
enroll_samples/
enroll_samples*/
# Speaker recognition belongs to the daemon, not the session app. Both work
# and are kept locally, but shipping them would put a biometric feature in a
# release that has no use for it - and would invite people to enroll voices
# with no gate built around the result yet.
voiceprint.py
enroll.py

# ---- per-install config ----
.env

# ---- daemon tier: held back until it's ready for scrutiny ----
# The session app (companion.py) does not import any of these - verified by
# dependency audit, not assumed. It reaches config/context/memory/prosody/
# session plus the audio stack, and context reaches archive. Nothing else.
daemon.py
talk.py
run.sh
state.py
thread.py
reflect.py
regulate.py
body.py

# ---- conversation and runtime state ----
transcripts/
session/
logs/
thoughts.jsonl
threads.json
threads_log.jsonl
state.json
regulate_obs.jsonl
prosody_baseline.json
body_state.json
body_events.jsonl
companion.sock
.miccheck.json
*.tmp

# ---- logs ----
*.log

# ---- installer artifacts ----
# install.sh writes these; all are per-machine.
# The generated llama-server launcher lives under --prefix (default
# <prefix>/start-llama.sh), outside the repo, so it needs no rule here.
.install-state
.install-hf.py
.venv/

# ---- audio: test output and anything captured ----
*.wav
*.raw

# ---- python ----
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.venv/
venv/

# ---- models and caches: never commit weights ----
*.gguf
*.onnx
*.pt
*.bin
models/
.cache/

# ---- explicitly DO ship ----
!core_memory.example.md
!origin.example.md
